1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:41,824
Incentive Alignment Bonds

8
00:01:42,724 --> 00:01:44,304
War bonds, but backwards.

9
00:01:45,124 --> 00:01:48,924
Your grandparents funded World War Two at roughly three percent returns.

10
00:01:49,444 --> 00:01:54,244
You fund disease eradication at two hundred and seventy-two percent.

11
00:01:54,244 --> 00:01:56,304
Same structure, fewer Nazis,

12
00:01:56,924 --> 00:01:57,564
better spreadsheet.

13
00:01:58,264 --> 00:02:02,544
Remember when your grandparents funded World War Two by buying war bonds?

14
00:02:02,884 --> 00:02:07,584
They got roughly three percent returns and a world without Nazis (mostly). Good deal.

15
00:02:07,584 --> 00:02:09,624
You're doing the same thing.

16
00:02:09,804 --> 00:02:12,164
Except instead of buying bonds to kill Nazis,

17
00:02:12,784 --> 00:02:14,464
you're buying bonds to kill diseases.

18
00:02:15,084 --> 00:02:16,504
War bonds, but backwards.

19
00:02:17,464 --> 00:02:18,424
The Core Problem:

20
00:02:18,964 --> 00:02:20,964
Good Ideas Die in Committee.

21
00:02:21,884 --> 00:02:23,544
Here's your species' fun puzzle:

22
00:02:24,124 --> 00:02:26,464
you know how to save millions of lives.

23
00:02:26,764 --> 00:02:28,744
You can measure exactly how many.

24
00:02:29,144 --> 00:02:30,044
You have the money.

25
00:02:30,564 --> 00:02:31,584
You don't do it.

26
00:02:31,584 --> 00:02:34,084
Not because your politicians are evil.

27
00:02:34,584 --> 00:02:36,724
Because your system is built so that:

28
00:02:36,724 --> 00:02:41,324
Politicians maximize reelection, status, and post-office careers,

29
00:02:41,964 --> 00:02:44,784
not "humans continuing to exist".

30
00:02:45,484 --> 00:02:50,244
Bureaucracies maximize budget and turf, not "speed of treatments".

31
00:02:51,124 --> 00:02:55,184
Lobbyists maximize client profits, not "global welfare".

32
00:02:55,984 --> 00:02:58,564
You don't fix this with awareness campaigns.

33
00:02:58,564 --> 00:03:03,044
You've been "raising awareness" for decades and everyone is still dying,

34
00:03:03,484 --> 00:03:05,504
but they're dying *aware*, so that's nice.

35
00:03:06,324 --> 00:03:08,024
You don't fix it with white papers.

36
00:03:08,604 --> 00:03:11,924
Politicians use white papers to stabilize wobbly tables.

37
00:03:12,564 --> 00:03:16,484
You fix it by changing what self-interest points at.

38
00:03:17,164 --> 00:03:22,524
On Wishonia, we used something very similar to bootstrap the whole transition

39
00:03:22,524 --> 00:03:25,704
four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years ago.

40
00:03:26,004 --> 00:03:29,764
We don't need them anymore (people do useful things because they're useful,

41
00:03:30,004 --> 00:03:33,944
which I realize sounds made up, but you also thought "washing your hands"

42
00:03:33,944 --> 00:03:37,244
sounded made up until eighteen forty-seven).

43
00:03:37,244 --> 00:03:38,004
The point is:

44
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:39,364
you need them now.

45
00:03:40,044 --> 00:03:44,324
This chapter describes how to legally bribe your politicians into doing

46
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:45,144
the right thing.

47
00:03:45,584 --> 00:03:49,304
(If at any point the numbers sound impossible, try the five questions.

48
00:03:49,944 --> 00:03:57,244
Find the one that's wrong. We'll wait.). Incentive Alignment Bonds (I.A.B.s):

49
00:03:57,244 --> 00:04:00,524
a financial instrument for paying for better governance without technically

50
00:04:00,524 --> 00:04:04,644
paying politicians, giving money to governments, or going to prison.

51
00:04:05,544 --> 00:04:10,144
Your one percent Treaty isn't constrained by physics, biology, or money.

52
00:04:10,644 --> 00:04:15,144
It's constrained by politics, which is like being constrained by your dog's

53
00:04:15,144 --> 00:04:19,464
opinion on quantum mechanics, except your dog can veto legislation.

54
00:04:20,384 --> 00:04:24,164
No politician wants to be the one who "cut the military."

55
00:04:24,444 --> 00:04:25,884
Even by one percent.

56
00:04:25,884 --> 00:04:28,464
Even if that one percent cures cancer.

57
00:04:29,004 --> 00:04:30,664
The attack ads write themselves:

58
00:04:31,624 --> 00:04:33,584
"Senator Johnson voted to WEAKEN AMERICA."

59
00:04:34,424 --> 00:04:37,724
Your system does exactly what it's incentivized to do.

60
00:04:37,924 --> 00:04:38,844
It's not broken.

61
00:04:39,344 --> 00:04:41,884
It's working perfectly at the wrong thing.

62
00:04:42,604 --> 00:04:43,104
The fix:

63
00:04:43,644 --> 00:04:45,724
tell every politician on Earth,

64
00:04:46,344 --> 00:04:50,404
"Vote for a one percent-style reform and you get better reelection odds

65
00:04:50,404 --> 00:04:53,224
and a Goldman Sachs board seat when you retire."

66
00:04:53,764 --> 00:04:54,684
No backroom deals.

67
00:04:55,084 --> 00:04:56,584
No suitcases of cash.

68
00:04:56,984 --> 00:04:58,944
Just a standing, public rule:

69
00:04:59,404 --> 00:05:03,604
do the objectively good thing, and the world systematically rewards you.

70
00:05:04,004 --> 00:05:06,024
Nobody has to become a better person.

71
00:05:06,384 --> 00:05:09,704
The money just circulates until diseases stop existing.

72
00:05:10,624 --> 00:05:13,304
How I.A.B.s Work (Four Steps).

73
00:05:14,184 --> 00:05:15,624
Not charity (doesn't scale).

74
00:05:16,204 --> 00:05:16,964
Not lobbying

75
00:05:17,624 --> 00:05:18,124
(slot taken).

76
00:05:18,644 --> 00:05:20,844
Not "paying politicians" (illegal,

77
00:05:21,624 --> 00:05:22,384
slot also taken).

78
00:05:22,384 --> 00:05:26,984
You work with the primates you have, not the primates you wish you had.

79
00:05:27,544 --> 00:05:28,924
The recipe has two steps.

80
00:05:29,544 --> 00:05:30,044
Step one:

81
00:05:30,344 --> 00:05:32,084
make the right thing profitable.

82
00:05:32,764 --> 00:05:33,264
Step two:

83
00:05:33,724 --> 00:05:34,224
wait.

84
00:05:34,564 --> 00:05:36,024
There is no Step three.

85
00:05:36,584 --> 00:05:41,144
On Wishonia, we spent four thousand years trying to add a Step three

86
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:46,724
(moral education, cultural reform, public shaming, interpretive dance).

87
00:05:47,384 --> 00:05:48,304
None of them worked.

88
00:05:48,764 --> 00:05:51,204
Step two always did the job by itself.

89
00:05:51,204 --> 00:05:53,124
Step one:

90
00:05:53,124 --> 00:05:54,664
Pick a Measurable Outcome.

91
00:05:55,764 --> 00:05:58,044
Measure funding flows, not health outcomes.

92
00:05:58,544 --> 00:06:02,704
You can't attribute a treatment breakthrough to any single country's funding.

93
00:06:03,144 --> 00:06:04,244
But you CAN measure:

94
00:06:04,244 --> 00:06:06,964
percent of military spending redirected,

95
00:06:07,664 --> 00:06:11,944
total dollars contributed, and politician votes on treaty passage.

96
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:14,824
Health improvements justify the policy.

97
00:06:15,884 --> 00:06:19,724
Funding flows are the scoreboard, because that's what politicians actually

98
00:06:19,724 --> 00:06:20,324
control.

99
00:06:21,164 --> 00:06:21,664
Step two:

100
00:06:22,064 --> 00:06:22,904
Raise Capital.

101
00:06:23,944 --> 00:06:27,804
Investors buy Incentive Alignment Bonds, or I.A.B.s.

102
00:06:28,584 --> 00:06:29,664
Capital sits in a trust.

103
00:06:30,084 --> 00:06:34,064
It pays out if and only if public-good targets are hit.

104
00:06:34,544 --> 00:06:37,704
Same structure as green bonds and catastrophe bonds.

105
00:06:38,404 --> 00:06:38,904
Step three:

106
00:06:39,344 --> 00:06:41,564
Reward Your Politicians (Indirectly).

107
00:06:41,564 --> 00:06:47,424
When a politician votes for a one percent-style policy and funding actually

108
00:06:47,424 --> 00:06:47,924
flows:

109
00:06:48,384 --> 00:06:49,904
Public Good Scores rise

110
00:06:50,584 --> 00:06:52,144
(published by independent rating orgs).

111
00:06:52,684 --> 00:06:57,504
Electoral support increases (independent campaigns favor high-scorers).

112
00:06:57,504 --> 00:07:03,104
Post-office opportunities unlock (fellowships, boards, speaking circuits).

113
00:07:03,644 --> 00:07:07,724
No money flows to politicians (see why this isn't bribery).

114
00:07:08,364 --> 00:07:13,104
What flows is reputation, electoral advantage, and career advancement.

115
00:07:13,764 --> 00:07:14,524
Step four:

116
00:07:14,524 --> 00:07:16,764
Watch Self-Interest Do the Rest.

117
00:07:17,384 --> 00:07:19,624
Your politicians' utility function is roughly:

118
00:07:19,624 --> 00:07:26,304
U equals probability of reelection, plus career advancement, plus post-office

119
00:07:26,304 --> 00:07:28,464
income, plus legacy.

120
00:07:29,284 --> 00:07:34,284
I.A.B.s make supporting one percent-equivalent policies strictly increase

121
00:07:34,284 --> 00:07:35,564
all four terms.

122
00:07:35,564 --> 00:07:37,304
No altruism required.

123
00:07:37,764 --> 00:07:42,964
"Maximize personal payoff" and "reduce suffering" become the same action.

124
00:07:43,464 --> 00:07:47,644
You've tricked your leaders into saving lives by making it the selfish thing

125
00:07:47,644 --> 00:07:48,204
to do.

126
00:07:48,644 --> 00:07:52,384
The Three-Layer Architecture (How to Not Go to Prison).

127
00:07:53,224 --> 00:07:56,764
You cannot legally say "support Bill X.Y.Z.

128
00:07:56,764 --> 00:07:58,604
one two three and get paid."

129
00:07:58,944 --> 00:07:59,624
That's bribery.

130
00:08:00,244 --> 00:08:05,084
But you can create a system where politicians who support a class of pro-social

131
00:08:05,084 --> 00:08:10,144
policies systematically get more of everything they want. The trick:

132
00:08:10,144 --> 00:08:13,504
rule-based, universal, announced in advance.

133
00:08:14,384 --> 00:08:14,884
Layer A:

134
00:08:15,364 --> 00:08:15,864
Scoring

135
00:08:16,264 --> 00:08:16,764
(Data Only).

136
00:08:17,284 --> 00:08:22,004
An independent org assigns each politician a Public Good Score based on

137
00:08:22,004 --> 00:08:24,211
votes, sponsorship, and funding flows.

138
00:08:24,211 --> 00:08:25,993
Scores cover a policy class (any greater than or equal to one percent military-to-health

139
00:08:25,993 --> 00:08:26,629
reallocation), not a specific bill.

140
00:08:26,629 --> 00:08:27,184
Public, rules-based, non-partisan.

141
00:08:27,964 --> 00:08:32,364
In the one percent Treaty materials, this domain-specific implementation

142
00:08:32,364 --> 00:08:34,584
is called the Treaty Support Score.

143
00:08:35,064 --> 00:08:39,244
(See the Senator Smith example for how scores translate to concrete payoffs.).

144
00:08:40,124 --> 00:08:40,624
Layer B:

145
00:08:41,184 --> 00:08:42,064
Electoral Benefits

146
00:08:42,724 --> 00:08:43,424
(Separate Actors).

147
00:08:44,504 --> 00:08:48,164
Independent PACs and five oh one c fours commit **in advance** to favor

148
00:08:48,164 --> 00:08:49,404
high-scoring politicians.

149
00:08:49,924 --> 00:08:50,424
The goal:

150
00:08:50,584 --> 00:08:54,884
make the Public Good Score as influential as Moody's credit ratings or N.R.A.

151
00:08:54,884 --> 00:08:55,384
grades.

152
00:08:55,884 --> 00:09:00,964
Moody's can downgrade a country and suddenly borrowing costs spike. N.R.A.

153
00:09:00,964 --> 00:09:04,124
grades already determine which politicians get funded.

154
00:09:04,844 --> 00:09:07,644
Same gun, different target. Layer C:

155
00:09:07,644 --> 00:09:11,424
Post-Office Careers (The Goldman Sachs Board Problem).

156
00:09:12,384 --> 00:09:15,364
Foundations and think tanks set eligibility rules:

157
00:09:15,864 --> 00:09:18,644
Public Good Score above X gets you W.H.O.

158
00:09:18,644 --> 00:09:20,424
boards and Aspen fellowships.

159
00:09:20,924 --> 00:09:25,144
Below X, you're explaining at dinner why you voted against curing diseases.

160
00:09:25,724 --> 00:09:29,574
The revolving door, but spinning toward "saved lives" instead of toward

161
00:09:29,574 --> 00:09:31,394
whoever paid the most lobbyists.

162
00:09:32,774 --> 00:09:33,814
Legal Entity Separation.

163
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:39,114
For the Scoring layer, a five oh one c three research organization handles

164
00:09:39,114 --> 00:09:44,294
metrics, dashboards, and public data, but cannot support or oppose candidates.

165
00:09:45,014 --> 00:09:50,114
For the Electoral layer, five oh one c fours, PACs, and Super PACs handle

166
00:09:50,114 --> 00:09:55,114
independent expenditures for high-scorers, but cannot coordinate with candidates.

167
00:09:55,114 --> 00:10:00,514
For the Post-office layer, foundations and think tanks set eligibility criteria,

168
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:04,054
but cannot condition grants on specific votes.

169
00:10:04,834 --> 00:10:09,474
Three separate entities that definitely don't coordinate but somehow all

170
00:10:09,474 --> 00:10:11,074
reward the same behavior.

171
00:10:11,774 --> 00:10:13,653
Your species invented this structure.

172
00:10:13,994 --> 00:10:18,533
It's genuinely one of your better ideas, which is a low bar, but still.

173
00:10:19,474 --> 00:10:20,694
Why This Isn't Bribery.

174
00:10:21,293 --> 00:10:24,033
Four reasons your lawyers will stop hyperventilating:

175
00:10:24,033 --> 00:10:26,734
No one is paid to break a duty.

176
00:10:27,394 --> 00:10:29,914
"Do your job better and we'll tell everyone you did."

177
00:10:30,374 --> 00:10:32,394
That's a performance review, not a bribe.

178
00:10:33,554 --> 00:10:35,694
Rules are universal and ex-ante.

179
00:10:35,694 --> 00:10:40,214
Same rules, all politicians, all parties, announced publicly in advance.

180
00:10:40,654 --> 00:10:42,334
No envelopes in parking garages.

181
00:10:43,134 --> 00:10:44,594
No money goes to politicians.

182
00:10:44,974 --> 00:10:46,354
They benefit indirectly:

183
00:10:46,974 --> 00:10:50,334
better scores, electoral support, nicer career options.

184
00:10:50,334 --> 00:10:55,254
This is how democracy was supposed to work before your species broke it.

185
00:10:55,754 --> 00:10:57,774
Scores are based on public voting records.

186
00:10:58,234 --> 00:10:59,194
Did they vote YES?

187
00:10:59,814 --> 00:11:01,574
Verifiable and ungameable.

188
00:11:02,074 --> 00:11:06,054
The ten percent fund flows automatically based on treasury inflows.

189
00:11:06,474 --> 00:11:06,974
Pure math.

190
00:11:08,154 --> 00:11:09,674
Bribery **corrupts** alignment.

191
00:11:10,274 --> 00:11:14,134
Incentive Alignment Bonds, or I.A.B.s **create** it.

192
00:11:14,134 --> 00:11:16,834
Wealthy actors already buy policy

193
00:11:17,634 --> 00:11:20,534
(pharma spends three hundred million dollars a year on lobbying,

194
00:11:21,374 --> 00:11:23,954
weapons manufacturers spend one hundred and twenty-seven million dollars

195
00:11:23,954 --> 00:11:24,754
a year).

196
00:11:25,194 --> 00:11:28,114
The question isn't "should money influence policy?"

197
00:11:28,474 --> 00:11:32,034
but "can you point the money at welfare instead of warfare?".

198
00:11:32,794 --> 00:11:35,954
Here's what makes this structurally different from current lobbying:

199
00:11:36,534 --> 00:11:39,774
in the current system, money and influence are inseparable.

200
00:11:40,254 --> 00:11:44,774
Give money, get influence over where the money goes, use that to get more

201
00:11:44,774 --> 00:11:45,274
money.

202
00:11:45,514 --> 00:11:48,834
The loop is opaque and self-reinforcing.

203
00:11:48,834 --> 00:11:50,394
I.A.B.s break the loop.

204
00:11:50,814 --> 00:11:54,514
Investors give money and get money back (ten percent revenue share).

205
00:11:54,974 --> 00:11:55,474
That's it.

206
00:11:55,874 --> 00:11:58,234
They don't decide which diseases get funded.

207
00:11:59,034 --> 00:12:02,154
Politicians get career incentives (ten percent).

208
00:12:02,154 --> 00:12:03,854
They don't touch the research budget.

209
00:12:04,674 --> 00:12:09,994
The remaining eighty percent flows to clinical trials via wishocratic allocation,

210
00:12:10,834 --> 00:12:14,654
controlled by direct democracy, not by the people who paid for it.

211
00:12:15,174 --> 00:12:19,534
The corruption is capped at twenty percent, transparent, and completely

212
00:12:19,534 --> 00:12:21,854
separated from the public goods funding.

213
00:12:22,774 --> 00:12:24,874
Name a government budget that can say the same.

214
00:12:25,834 --> 00:12:26,514
Worked Example:

215
00:12:26,514 --> 00:12:28,994
How Senator Smith Votes Yes.

216
00:12:30,394 --> 00:12:35,194
Abstract mechanisms are great for economists and incomprehensible to everyone

217
00:12:35,194 --> 00:12:35,714
who matters.

218
00:12:35,714 --> 00:12:42,254
Here's how I.A.B.s work on an actual human politician (a creature that navigates

219
00:12:42,254 --> 00:12:45,854
entirely by self-interest, like a moth but with a pension).

220
00:12:47,254 --> 00:12:48,094
The Scoring System.

221
00:12:48,894 --> 00:12:53,394
Each politician gets a Public Good Score based on their voting record (like

222
00:12:53,394 --> 00:12:55,734
a credit score for your soul, except useful):

223
00:12:56,574 --> 00:13:01,054
For a bill to increase percentage reallocation to a one percent Treaty Fund,

224
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:06,334
a yes vote is plus fifteen and a no vote is minus fifteen.

225
00:13:06,334 --> 00:13:11,334
To protect existing funding, a yes vote is plus ten and a no vote is minus

226
00:13:11,334 --> 00:13:12,274
ten.

227
00:13:12,274 --> 00:13:16,954
To expand the treaty to more countries, a yes vote is plus ten and a no

228
00:13:16,954 --> 00:13:18,594
vote is minus ten.

229
00:13:18,594 --> 00:13:24,134
To cut funding or percentage, a yes vote is minus twenty and a no vote is

230
00:13:24,134 --> 00:13:25,774
plus five.

231
00:13:25,774 --> 00:13:27,834
Your score determines what you get:

232
00:13:28,394 --> 00:13:33,354
A score of seventy-five or higher gets you plus two million dollars in PAC

233
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:37,614
spending, a Tier One post-office career such as W.H.O.

234
00:13:37,614 --> 00:13:42,139
boards or Aspen fellowships, and an annual income of five hundred thousand

235
00:13:42,139 --> 00:13:43,334
dollars or more.

236
00:13:43,914 --> 00:13:47,974
A score of sixty to seventy-four gets you plus five hundred thousand dollars

237
00:13:47,974 --> 00:13:52,454
in PAC spending, a Tier Two post-office career like Brookings,

238
00:13:53,234 --> 00:13:58,565
R.A.N.D., or university chairs, and an annual income of two hundred to four

239
00:13:58,565 --> 00:13:59,774
hundred thousand dollars.

240
00:13:59,774 --> 00:14:04,854
A score of fifty to fifty-nine gets you zero dollars in PAC spending, a

241
00:14:04,854 --> 00:14:09,974
Tier Three standard revolving door post-office career, and an annual income

242
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:13,256
of one hundred and fifty to three hundred thousand dollars.

243
00:14:13,256 --> 00:14:17,234
A score of forty to forty-nine results in five hundred thousand dollars

244
00:14:17,234 --> 00:14:22,514
in PAC spending for your opponent, a Tier Three post-office career, and

245
00:14:22,514 --> 00:14:24,448
an annual income of one hundred and fifty to three hundred thousand dollars.

246
00:14:24,448 --> 00:14:25,529
A score below forty results in two million dollars in PAC spending for your

247
00:14:25,529 --> 00:14:26,533
opponent, a Tier Three post-office career, and an annual income of one hundred

248
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:27,074
and fifty to three hundred thousand dollars.

249
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:27,894
In short:

250
00:14:28,474 --> 00:14:33,554
high scorers get millions in PAC support and access to the best post-office

251
00:14:33,554 --> 00:14:34,054
careers.

252
00:14:34,714 --> 00:14:37,874
Low scorers watch that same money go to their opponents.

253
00:14:38,554 --> 00:14:41,634
It's like a video game skill tree, except the X.P.

